# This repository uses CRLF line endings throughout (decision of record,
# see README.md). Without this file, git's own line-ending normalization
# is a silent trap: a checkout on a platform/config where `core.autocrlf`
# behaves differently can rewrite every text file's line endings on
# clone, and a contributor's local `core.autocrlf=true` can silently
# convert CRLF back to LF on commit — in both cases producing a tree that
# no longer matches what every fixture in this repo assumes, without any
# diff showing why. `text=false` on every extension pins the raw bytes:
# git stores and checks out exactly what's committed, regardless of
# platform or a contributor's global git config.
#
# This isn't cosmetic. `packages/engine/test/fixtures/**` includes gold
# fixtures whose expected output depends on the exact line-ending
# sequence between wrapped lines (see `docs/adapters.md`, "CRLF handling"
# for the concrete bug this exact gap caused). A `.gitattributes`-less
# checkout is the single most likely way to silently reintroduce it.

* -text
